(763133, 83614, 3032, '<td valign="top">Your topic, security &amp; ''dead'' airplanes, is well portrayed with this composition. That extra ring of barb wire looks pretty fresh and the field has the elements of what people around the world know of the American aeroplane graveyards (Arizona, my guess is near Tucson?). The light is a bit harsh, could be better to wait for an opportunity with less sun power, longer shadows and a bit warmer light.<br/>On a side note; I don''t think this field is for dead airplanes, but a cheap parking lot for planes that have no use at this moment but are still fully functional and can be flown out with little preparation. I know the KLM parks some of their planes in the US desert in the winter.</td>', 'Your topic, security & ''dead'' airplanes, is well portrayed with this composition. That extra ring of barb wire looks pretty fresh and the field has the elements of what people around the world know of the American aeroplane graveyards (Arizona, my guess is near Tucson?). The light is a bit harsh, could be better to wait for an opportunity with less sun power, longer shadows and a bit warmer light.On a side note; I don''t think this field is for dead airplanes, but a cheap parking lot for planes that have no use at this moment but are still fully functional and can be flown out with little preparation. I know the KLM parks some of their planes in the US desert in the winter.', '2004-06-14 18:37:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(763135, 83518, 4159, '<td valign="top">NIce car, but the picture itself isn''t that interesting.  Possibly a different setting?</td>', 'NIce car, but the picture itself isn''t that interesting.  Possibly a different setting?', '2004-06-14 18:41:48.000000', NULL, 1),
