(769383, 83485, 1009, '<td valign="top">I like the POV and sharpness on this one. I also like the sky. One of my highest scores of the week, a 7.</td>', 'I like the POV and sharpness on this one. I also like the sky. One of my highest scores of the week, a 7.', '2004-06-19 07:30:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(769384, 83576, 1009, '<td valign="top">I like the black and white/sepia look to this one. I find the border somewhat distracting though. Nice crop on the image. I like that you''ve included the name... good job.</td>', 'I like the black and white/sepia look to this one. I find the border somewhat distracting though. Nice crop on the image. I like that you''ve included the name... good job.', '2004-06-19 07:31:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(769385, 83493, 8860, '<td valign="top">Lovely car. Blur is OK but looks like it''s had some obvious PS help. The wing mirror appears to be in parking mode so I assume you spin-blurred the wheels. Subtlety is the key here - ensure that your selection is featherd by a pixel or two round the car body to avoid halos. I find it easier to motion blur an entire duplicate layer then mask in/out the areas that aren''t wanted. This avoids seams and joins appearing.</td>', 'Lovely car. Blur is OK but looks like it''s had some obvious PS help. The wing mirror appears to be in parking mode so I assume you spin-blurred the wheels. Subtlety is the key here - ensure that your selection is featherd by a pixel or two round the car body to avoid halos. I find it easier to motion blur an entire duplicate layer then mask in/out the areas that aren''t wanted. This avoids seams and joins appearing.', '2004-06-19 07:31:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(769386, 83133, 1009, '<td valign="top">I''ll give you an extra point because your alternate title was funny enough to make me laugh. Photo itself is so-so  :-)<br/> <br/>Thanks for the cheer-up...</td>', 'I''ll give you an extra point because your alternate title was funny enough to make me laugh. Photo itself is so-so  :-) Thanks for the cheer-up...', '2004-06-19 07:32:34.000000', NULL, 1),
