(771367, 83166, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tyt2000:</b></div><hr/><i> Paul, why take a photo out of your car''s window? I suggest putting more thought into your composition :)<br/> <br/>Good luck... </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Because I was driving to work, in the left-most of three lanes of merging traffic, and the helicopter was only going to be there for a moment. Believe me, if I could have set up traffic cones and my tripod I would have radioed the pilot to circle around and come in again from a better angle ... :)<br/> <br/>This is an opportunistic, photojournalistic-type shot (more suitable for this week!) and is obviously not "composed" in the usual sense. In retrospect, I agree with the people who suggested tighter cropping to eliminate clutter and put more emphasis on what part of the helicopter <b>is</b> visible. Still, this is one of the types of photography I do ... sometimes it works and sometimes it doesn''t. Sometimes I think it can be a decent photo, but not necessarily "Art" for the living room wall.</td>', 'Originally posted by tyt2000: Paul, why take a photo out of your car''s window? I suggest putting more thought into your composition :) Good luck...  Because I was driving to work, in the left-most of three lanes of merging traffic, and the helicopter was only going to be there for a moment. Believe me, if I could have set up traffic cones and my tripod I would have radioed the pilot to circle around and come in again from a better angle ... :) This is an opportunistic, photojournalistic-type shot (more suitable for this week!) and is obviously not "composed" in the usual sense. In retrospect, I agree with the people who suggested tighter cropping to eliminate clutter and put more emphasis on what part of the helicopter is visible. Still, this is one of the types of photography I do ... sometimes it works and sometimes it doesn''t. Sometimes I think it can be a decent photo, but not necessarily "Art" for the living room wall.', '2004-06-21 12:16:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(771421, 83557, 13688, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments.  As much as I''d like to think our police officers here in Tampa would love to lend a hand to a photographer in need...  I believe me crawling around the cars during a traffic stop would be cause for guns to be drawn.  Luckily this just appeared that way.  Though I must say it was a good catch.  There was a major accident on the road and the police car was blocking others from leaving that particular parking lot.  The slick 50''s auto just happened to be in a spot in front of it.  Sorry, to disappoint anyone who thought the shot was the outcome of a high speed pursuit.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-06-21 11:55:21.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the comments.  As much as I''d like to think our police officers here in Tampa would love to lend a hand to a photographer in need...  I believe me crawling around the cars during a traffic stop would be cause for guns to be drawn.  Luckily this just appeared that way.  Though I must say it was a good catch.  There was a major accident on the road and the police car was blocking others from leaving that particular parking lot.  The slick 50''s auto just happened to be in a spot in front of it.  Sorry, to disappoint anyone who thought the shot was the outcome of a high speed pursuit.', '2004-06-21 12:54:40.000000', '2004-06-21 12:55:21.000000', 0),
(771430, 83557, 13688, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Xarthan:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/> <br/>haha yeah afterwards he was like, hey officer can you take off your plates and let me take a picture?<br/> <br/>congrats! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks...actually plates aren''t displayed on the front of cars in Florida, only in the back.  Not good for catching cars that are trying to run you over, only ones that try to do it backing up ;)</td>', 'Originally posted by Xarthan:  haha yeah afterwards he was like, hey officer can you take off your plates and let me take a picture? congrats!   Thanks...actually plates aren''t displayed on the front of cars in Florida, only in the back.  Not good for catching cars that are trying to run you over, only ones that try to do it backing up ;)', '2004-06-21 13:01:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(771439, 82512, 12319, '<td valign="top">Beautifully shot, good to see someone taking time to get a particular shot, well deserved ribbon. Personally, I would have toned down the tungsten lighting (yellow/orange) effect. Else wise, flawless.</td>', 'Beautifully shot, good to see someone taking time to get a particular shot, well deserved ribbon. Personally, I would have toned down the tungsten lighting (yellow/orange) effect. Else wise, flawless.', '2004-06-21 13:11:04.000000', NULL, 0),
