(781702, 83285, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>It''s a very interesting photo and before getting this to critique I had seen your post in the forum of both this and the full color version.  I''m guessing you used Photoshop. I''m not sure if photoshop offers the sepia  toning that PSP does, but that would have given you that nostolgic look without the pink sky.  Which really the pink sky is your only downfall to this photo.  The sky just grabs your attention and takes away from the caboose.  Personally, I would have either used sepia toning or went with the natural colors.  The sky just takes away from the rest of the photo.  <br/> <br/>Overall your focus is good as is the composition, and it does fit the challenge well.  Keep up the good work and just watch out for distracting elements that take away from your subject.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', 'Critique Club It''s a very interesting photo and before getting this to critique I had seen your post in the forum of both this and the full color version.  I''m guessing you used Photoshop. I''m not sure if photoshop offers the sepia  toning that PSP does, but that would have given you that nostolgic look without the pink sky.  Which really the pink sky is your only downfall to this photo.  The sky just grabs your attention and takes away from the caboose.  Personally, I would have either used sepia toning or went with the natural colors.  The sky just takes away from the rest of the photo.   Overall your focus is good as is the composition, and it does fit the challenge well.  Keep up the good work and just watch out for distracting elements that take away from your subject. Anna', '2004-06-27 21:42:00.000000', NULL, 0),
